world war one was a war of losers even  the winners lost  amongst the countries which did lose  perhaps the greatest loser was the  kingdom of hungary  which lost 70 percent of its land and  about 65 percent of its population  and given that many in the hungarian  government were opposed to the war  at least at first why was hungary in  particular punished so severely  so at the outbreak of the war the  kingdom of hungary was made up of many  different peoples many of whom frankly  wanted out and as such for those in  charge maintaining hungary's integrity  was more important than any territorial  conquest  as opposed to the austrian half of the  empire that sought territory in italy  and in poland and was overwhelmingly  pro-war  there are many reasons why the antarette  pushed for the breakup of the kingdom of  hungary  the first was that this wasn't a  negotiation but a dictat  countries that lose wars as completely  as austria-hungary did weren't in a  position to negotiate over the terms  the second reason was that they had made  many promises of national sovereignty  during the war to groups like the czechs  and the polish  which was in return for these people  launching rebellions or simply refusing  to fight for the empires that they  currently lived in  the antante also assured countries like  romania and serbia that their  territorial claims on the habsburg  empire would be respected  and so that's why places like  transylvania were bargained away  irrespective of the hungarian  government's wishes  now this wasn't a case of the anton  presenting some united front  britain was fairly unconcerned about  what territory hungary would keep and  what its allies in the region would  receive  since its primary concern was the  ottoman empire in germany and what it  could get from them  the united states was a big supporter of  self-determination as a principle but  its leadership had no experience nor  much interest in dictating the borders  of countries in southeastern europe  the main architects of hungary's breakup  were italy mostly for its own  territorial ambitions and notably  france the french were entirely focused  on the decades that were to come after  the war  and france wished to build a strong  alliance with the countries in the  region aimed at the new soviet union and  any resurgent germany  and making sure that these potential  allies got what they wanted from hungary  was a big part of that plan  so that's all seth would right well no  the hungarians had hoped that the front  lines at the armistice would be where  hungary's new borders would be  yet as the treaty of trianon was being  negotiated by the anton the liberal  hungarian government collapsed and it  was replaced by a social democratic one  which had made an agreement with the  communist party  and when they were in power the  communists swiftly purged everyone else  and declared that hungary was a  communist state and one which wouldn't  accept any territorial losses  something it proved by swiftly invading  czechoslovakia and starting another war  with romania  for the anton this focused minds and  made it clear that the hungarians didn't  accept their defeat  and that they would likely seek to fight  again as soon as they were able to in  order to reclaim their old territory  this fact terrified the nations on  hungary's borders and so they demanded  via the french that the terms be harsh  the communist government collapsed in  late 1919 and after this the french took  a much more lenient approach to the  hungarians and sought to offer them this  so long as they agree to an anti-soviet  alliance the reason being that the  soviets were busy invading poland and  the french were terrified of what they  could do if they won  these plans went nowhere because the  polish managed to defeat the soviets on  their own  and the nations in southeastern europe  wouldn't countenance anything except  absolute humiliation for hungary  and so alongside broad restrictions on  the size of its military hungary lost  most of its population and its territory  and the country took on the shape that  it has today  i hope you enjoyed this episode and  thank you for watching with a special  thanks to my patrons  james bissonette kelly moneymaker alex  schwinn mr wolf captain cydog adam's  daughter  skye chappelle marvin cassell aaron the  white mo  james castaneda jordan longley jerry  landon gustav swan rasheed ali winston k  wood boogery wiggely  spinning three plates copper tone maggie  paskowski spencer lightfoot  matthew shipley robert wetzel corso  wolff the mc whopper anthony beckett  marcus asner lil brepentisi and charles  the first
 

